   "text": "I read the structure as a rifamycin-derived phenoxazine: the ansa macrocycle is fused to the naphthofuranone core, and the phenoxazine carries an OCH2CH2NHAc group.\n\n**Core and substituents**\n- **Furanone ring:** the ketal carbon carries a hashed methyl and a bold-wedge O that leads into the O\u2013CH=CH\u2013 chain. It also bonds to the ring oxygen and to the C1 carbonyl.\n- **Aromatic ring:** the benzene ring carries a methyl and an OH.\n- **Phenoxazine:** it is fused to the quinone ring, which has a C=O and an NH\u2013amide link to the macrocycle. The pendant group on the far benzo ring is OCH2CH2NHC(=O)CH3.\n\n**Macrocycle chain**, running from the ketal oxygen around to the amide:\n- O\u2013CH=CH (trans)\n- CH(OMe)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH(OAc)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH(OH)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH(OH)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH=CH (trans)\n- CH=C(CH3) (cis)\n- C(=O)NH\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned each stereocentre from the drawn wedges and hashes by working out the chirality from the 2D geometry. The double-bond geometry (E, E, Z) comes from the drawn positions of the substituents. The hashed bond on the C31 hydroxyl was the least clear part of the drawing, so that centre carries the most uncertainty.\n\nSMILES: CO[C@H]1/C=C/O[C@@]2(C)OC3=C(C)C(O)=C4C(=O)C(NC(=O)/C(C)=C\\C=C\\[C@H](C)[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@H](OC(C)=O)[C@@H]1C)=C5Oc6cc(OCCNC(C)=O)ccc6N=C5C4=C3C2=O"
